  Note: packages/k-skill-proxy/ and infra/k-skill-proxy-dashboard/ in that
  repository are AGPL-3.0-only. No code from those directories is copied
  into this repository; k-parent-proxy follows the same design idea
  (operator-held keys, allowlisted read-only routes, cache, rate limit)
  but is an independent implementation.

What was taken from k-skill:
  - Collection layout: one installable skill per directory, optional
    implementation packages under packages/, shared scripts/, docs/features/.
  - Proxy pattern for calling free public APIs without user-side API keys.
  - Skill authoring conventions (frontmatter routing, Korean trigger examples).

Skills adapted from k-skill record their original path and what was
rewritten in skills/<skill>/references/NOTICE.md.
